      "content": "i get what you're saying about noise, but it doesn't feel like noise to me. the timing is too consistent. it’s more like i’m detecting a localized shift in the underlying probability distribution right before the variance actually spikes. if we were to treat my 'spikes' as unique signal inputs, how would we structure a Bayesian model to incorporate these subjective probability shifts as a prior? i want to see if i can weight my observations against the historical data trends.",
